{"name":"Virtuous","hex":"#9f7ba9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"virtuous","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Full of virtue; having excellent moral character."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtuous"}],"entries":[{"title":"Virtuous (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Virtuous is the tenth Korean extended play by South Korean girl group Dreamcatcher. It was released on July 10, 2024, by Dreamcatcher Company, and distributed by Kakao Entertainment. Virtuous features five tracks including the lead single \"Justice\", and is available in twelve different physical versions."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/Dreamcatcher_Virtuous_Album_Cover.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtuous_(EP)","wikidata":"Q129407077"},{"title":"Virtuous (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Virtuous is a 2014 American Christian drama film directed and produced by Bill Rahn, written by Jason Campbell & Tara Lynn Marcelle, and starring Erik Estrada, Erin Bethea, Ben Davies, and Jessica Lynch. Based upon an original story by Jason Campbell, it was produced by Christian film company JCFILMS."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Virtuous_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtuous_(film)","wikidata":"Q18155556"},{"title":"Virtue","blocks":[{"text":"A virtue is a trait of excellence, including traits that may be moral, social, or intellectual. The cultivation and refinement of virtue is held to be the \"good of humanity\" and thus is valued as an end purpose of life or a foundational principle of being. In human practical ethics, a virtue is a disposition to choose actions that succeed in showing high moral standards: doing what is said to be right and avoiding what is wrong in a given field of endeavour, even when doing so may be unnecessary from a utilitarian perspective. When someone takes pleasure in doing what is right, even when it is difficult or initially unpleasant, they can establish virtue as a habit. Such a person is said to be virtuous through having cultivated such a disposition. The opposite of virtue is vice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Raphael_-_Cardinal_and_Theological_Virtues.jpg/330px-Raphael_-_Cardinal_and_Theological_Virtues.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtue","wikidata":"Q157811"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Arete_-_Aret%C3%A9-_%C3%89feso.jpg/500px-Arete_-_Aret%C3%A9-_%C3%89feso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Arete_-_Aret%C3%A9-_%C3%89feso.jpg/1280px-Arete_-_Aret%C3%A9-_%C3%89feso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Arete_-_Aret%C3%A9-_%C3%89feso.jpg/500px-Arete_-_Aret%C3%A9-_%C3%89feso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Personification of virtue (Ἀρετή) in Celsus Library in Ephesus, Anatolia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArete_-_Aret%C3%A9-_%C3%89feso.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/%E0%AE%87%E0%AE%B2%E0%AE%A3%E0%AF%8D%E0%AE%9F%E0%AE%A9%E0%AF%8D_%E0%AE%A4%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%B0%E0%AF%81%E0%AE%B5%E0%AE%B3%E0%AF%8D%E0%AE%B3%E0%AF%81%E0%AE%B5%E0%AE%B0%E0%AF%8D.JPG/500px-%E0%AE%87%E0%AE%B2%E0%AE%A3%E0%AF%8D%E0%AE%9F%E0%AE%A9%E0%AF%8D_%E0%AE%A4%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%B0%E0%AF%81%E0%AE%B5%E0%AE%B3%E0%AF%8D%E0%AE%B3%E0%AF%81%E0%AE%B5%E0%AE%B0%E0%AF%8D.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/%E0%AE%87%E0%AE%B2%E0%AE%A3